course: dictionary
lesson: 9238
title: Feelings in a word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how someone speaks or acts. Soothingly is an adverb, so it tells you how something is done. Read the clues around it. «Well then, it isn't, it isn't,» says the Mole soothingly. The Mole has just been arguing, so his words must be gentle and calm, not sharp.
explain: Ask what the speaker is trying to do. A nurse speaks soothingly to a child who is scared of an injection. Her voice is calm and gentle, so the child feels less worried. If you swap in "calmly and gently" and the sentence still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
explain: Soothingly can also describe sounds and touches. Water lapped soothingly against the boat, and music played soothingly in the background. Here it means calm and gentle. The water and the music are not upset.
fact: Soothingly is an adverb, so it describes how an action is done.
fact: «Soothingly» means in a calm, gentle way that makes someone feel less upset, worried or in pain.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, Rat talks soothingly to Mole when Mole is frightened or homesick.
fact: Soothing words, sounds and touches all share the idea of calm and gentleness.
fact: To check a word, read the clues around it, then swap in your own meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The nurse spoke soothingly to the frightened child.» What does soothingly mean? | In a loud, angry way | In a hurried, rude way | In a sleepy, bored way | *In a calm, gentle way
exercise: «The water lapped soothingly against the boat.» What does soothingly describe? | The colour of the water | How loud the boat's engine was | How fast the boat sailed | *How the water moved, gently and calmly
exercise: «Well then, it isn't, it isn't,» says the Mole soothingly. Find and copy the word that tells how the Mole speaks. | Well | Mole | isn't | *soothingly
test: Rat speaks to Mole soothingly when Mole is homesick. What is soothingly helping Mole with? | Feeling more excited | Feeling sleepy | *Feeling less upset | Feeling hungry
test: Which word is closest in meaning to soothingly? | angrily | *gently | noisily | rudely
exam: What is the Mole's purpose when he speaks soothingly to the Rat? | To make the Rat laugh loudly | *To keep the peace and calm things down | To ask the Rat for the time | To start a fight
